# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PRIVATE TREES — this repo is PUBLIC. These must never enter it.
#
# These were previously excluded ONLY by `.git/info/exclude`, which is
# per-clone, untracked, and NOT recreated by `git clone`. A fresh clone
# followed by `git add -A` would therefore have staged the entire private
# business SSoT and the local secrets vault into a public repository.
# Verified 2026-07-26: nothing has ever leaked — every path below is clean
# across the whole history. This is preventive, and it travels with the repo.
# `.git/info/exclude` is intentionally left in place as a second layer.
# [pipeline F-6]
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/
knowledge/
company/
scripts/
CLAUDE.md

# Generated git bundles — the code's second offsite copy [pipeline F-7b].
# Regenerated by .claude/scripts/backup-knowledge.ps1 on every run; never
# committed (a repo containing a bundle of itself is a recursion nobody needs).
.bundles/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECRETS — never commit. All credentials live in .claude/ (above)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.cowork-private/
*.env
!*.env.example
.dev.vars
!.dev.vars.example
*.pem
*.key
*-service-account*.json
secrets.*

# ── Android/Apple app-signing — NEVER commit (a leaked signing key + password lets
#    anyone publish malicious updates as you; public repo = permanent exposure) ──
release-keystore/
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12
key.properties
KEYSTORE_*.txt
KEYSTORE_B64*
*.mobileprovision
*.cer
AuthKey_*.p8

# ── App live config (dart-define-from-file; non-secret but env-specific) ──
apps/subly/config/*.json
!apps/subly/config/*.example.json

# ── Flutter / Dart (GLOBAL — survives app/→apps/ move) ──
**/.dart_tool/
**/.flutter-plugins
**/.flutter-plugins-dependencies
**/build/
**/.packages
**/pubspec.lock
**/ios/Pods/
**/android/.gradle/
**/android/local.properties
**/*/GeneratedPluginRegistrant.*
**/windows/flutter/ephemeral/
**/linux/flutter/ephemeral/
**/macos/Flutter/ephemeral/

# ── Node / Cloudflare / web (GLOBAL) ──
**/node_modules/
# Worker lockfiles ARE tracked (reversed 2026-07-26, [pipeline F-8]).
#
# The previous rule ignored them, reasoning that "the services/* lanes run
# `npm install`, not `npm ci`, so a committed lock buys nothing". That is
# circular — the lock bought nothing *because* nothing used it — and it was
# written before `deploy-workers.yml` existed. The consequence was live: the CI
# dry-run that "proved" a Worker deploy and the deploy itself each ran their own
# `npm install`, minutes apart, against caret ranges. Whichever version won that
# race is what reached production, holding the credential that applies D1
# migrations. `git checkout <sha> && npm install` could never reproduce a
# shipped build.
#
# Both service lockfiles are now committed and every lane uses `npm ci`.
**/.wrangler/
**/dist/
**/_site/
coverage/

# ── COMMITTED generated design tokens (Style Dictionary outputs) — re-include ──
!/packages/tokens/build/
!/packages/tokens/build/**

# ── Pub workspace root artifacts ──
/.dart_tool/
# Root workspace lock IS committed (reproducible app builds; apps/subly is a
# resolution: workspace member). Member locks stay ignored via **/pubspec.lock above.
!/pubspec.lock

# ── IDE / Melos ──
/.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/

# ── OS / editor ──
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log

# ── Internal planning docs (kept OUT of the public repo) ──
/Backend Research - Firebase vs Cloudflare (July 2026).md
/Subscription tracker app design/
/NIKATRU_GAP_ANALYSIS*.md

# ── strategy docs -> private nikatru-company repo ──
/PROJECT_STATE.md
/NIKATRU_MASTER_REQUIREMENTS.md

# Throwaway app stamped by the brick CI lane (P0.7)
apps/probe/
services/probe-api/

# Mason local brick cache
.mason/
mason-lock.json

# Flutter platform build outputs (scaffolded 2026-07-25)
**/windows/flutter/ephemeral/
**/linux/flutter/ephemeral/
**/macos/Flutter/ephemeral/
